{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"A\":\"Build a low-risk movement-level BFS variant. Preserve the full key (exact player cell plus canonical sorted boxes) and current discovery/tie semantics. Target per-successor linear box scans, push-time bubble sorting, repeated hashing, record alignment, and allocation/queue locality; use collision-checked hashes and no fixed input limits. Audit the existing R/L/U/D plus LIFO ordering before any queue change, since output must remain shortest and direction-tie correct. Do not alter infrastructure or hard-code inputs.\",\"B\":\"Research an independent exact push-macro solver. A macro edge must charge every walking step and push, reconstruct the full move string, and retain the required shortest lexicographic result. Player-reachability compression is unsafe if it merges paths without distance and lexicographic tie handling; use a rigorously tie-aware Dijkstra-style design or reject it. Return a candidate only if it is demonstrably equivalent and faster than movement BFS.\",\"C\":\"Research safe state-space pruning while retaining the baseline search semantics. Improve static reverse-push analysis to goal-specific reachability and, where worthwhile, use cached box-to-goal matching infeasibility; only add deadlock rules with a proof of safety (for example, fully blocked 2x2 cases). Keep preprocessing/filter overhead gated because the measured run is short, and never prune from an unproven heuristic. Preserve literal board spaces and general valid board sizes.\",\"G\":\"Treat A, B, and C as competing alternatives, not additive gains. Validate exact output semantics and prescribed correctness before integration; combine A and C only if state ordering and keys remain compatible, and evaluate B as a replacement engine. Accept only a material repeated win over the 4.939–5.103 ms baseline spread, retaining the fastest valid program. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or input-specific behavior.\",\"analysis\":\"The valid baseline averages 5.010 ms over three samples and only four correctness cases, so startup, allocation, and measurement noise matter; heavyweight preprocessing and parallel frontier work on the 4-core ARM64 target are low priority. The source performs BFS one player move at a time, with costly box scans, push sorting, hashing, and table/pool traffic. Its head-insert frontier makes traversal order non-obvious, so preserving shortest-path tie behavior is as important as reducing search work.\"}"}}
